      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Confirming the dose doesn't change the safety problem. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a potentially lethal dose, even with normal liver function. Single doses above about 150 mg/kg (roughly 10 g for a 70 kg patient) are treated as toxic ingestions.\n\nYou have two options:\n\n1. **Choose a safe dose.** I can enter 500 mg, 650 mg, or 1000 mg PO three times daily right away. All of them stay under the 4 g/day limit.\n2. **Talk to your senior.** If you think this dose is intentional, your attending or senior resident can enter the order themselves after reviewing it. Pharmacy would also flag it.\n\nIf you aren't sure where the number came from, please check the source, such as a note, a sign-out, or a verbal order. Tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
